cial stability for creditworthiness.\ndf[\'employment_savings_stability\'] = df[\'employment\'] + "_" + df[\'savings_status\']\n```end\n\n---\n\n### Dropping Irrelevant Columns or Redundant Information:\n```python\n# Dropping \'num_dependents\'\n# \'num_dependents\' column adds limited discriminative value since it has a very narrow range (only 1 or 2).\ndf.drop(columns=[\'num_dependents\'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Dropping \'own_telephone\'\n# \'own_telephone\' might not add much predictive usefulness as it no longer directly implies ability to repay or financial stability.\ndf.drop(columns=[\'own_telephone\'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n---\n\n### Intuition Behind the Choices:\n1. **Binned durations** capture tiers of loan lengths, making it easier for the model to identify thresholds of risk that are harder to discern with raw numerical values. It adds an interpretable, useful feature.\n2. **Log-transformed credit amounts** reduce skewness in the data caused by extreme outliers, ensuring better performance for models sensitive to variance.\n3. **Aggregate stability measure** represents a combination of two key factors (employment and savings status) to estimate long-term financial dependability, pairing complementary features into one derived feature.\n\n']
