n_telephone'], inplace=True)\nend\n\n---\n\n### Intuition Behind the Choices:\n1. Binned durations capture tiers of loan lengths, making it easier for the model to identify thresholds of risk that are harder to discern with raw numerical values. It adds an interpretable, useful feature.\n2. Log-transformed credit amounts reduce skewness in the data caused by extreme outliers, ensuring better performance for models sensitive to variance.\n3. Aggregate stability measure represents a combination of two key factors (employment and savings status) to estimate long-term financial dependability, pairing complementary features into one derived feature.", "python\n# Feature name: credit_amount_to_income_ratio\n# Feature description: Ratio of credit amount to installment commitment, approximating the loan amount relative to disposable income.\n# Usefulness: This feature provides a normalized measure of the borrower's loan burden. A higher ratio may indicate excessive borrowing relative to their income, which is a key factor in assessing creditworthiness.\ndf['credit_amount_to_income_ratio'] = df['credit_amount'] / (df['installment_commitment'] + 1e-9)\nend\n\npython\n# Feature name: employment_duration_stability\n# Feature description: Encodes employment duration into a numeric ranking (e.g., unemployed=0, <1 year=1, 1<=X<4=2, 4<=X<7=3, >=7=4).\n# Usefulness: This transformation converts the categorical 'employment' feature into a numerical representation that captures stability and enables the model to learn relationships between employment duration and credit risk.\nemployment_mapping = {'unemployed': 0, '<1': 1, '1<=X<4': 2, '4<=X<7': 3, '>=7': 4}\ndf['employment_duration_stability'] = df['employment'].map(employment_mapping)\nend\n\npython\n# Feature name: savings_score\n# Feature description: Converts savings_status categories into a numeric ranking (e.g., no known savings=0, <100=1, 100<=X<500=2, 500<=X<1000=3, >=1000=4).\n# Usefulness: By quantifying savings status, th